	quest.2101000000000001.title: "Start Somewhere"
	quest.2101000000000001.quest_subtitle: "Your first workstation"
	quest.2101000000000001.quest_desc: ["Craft a crafting table. Meridian does not define your backstory — the world is already here, and surviving it is up to you."]
	quest.2101000000000002.title: "Stone at Hand"
	quest.2101000000000002.quest_subtitle: "Первые материалы через инструмент с блюпринтом"
	quest.2101000000000002.quest_desc: [
		"Для зачёта собери 16 булыжника в обычном инвентаре. Каменная ванильная кирка не требуется: её рецепт в этой сборке отключён."
		"Шаг 1. Найди в JEI блюпринт кирки Silent Gear и открой его рецепт. Сделай шаблон и используй совместимые деревянные материалы для первой рабочей части; собери инструмент по рецептам JEI."
		"Шаг 2. Добудь камень деревянной киркой и подбери выпавший булыжник. Сначала накопи 16 блоков, чтобы задача успела засчитаться."
		"Шаг 3. Через блюпринт сделай каменную рабочую часть и собери либо обнови кирку по рецепту сборки. Дерево и камень проходят через верстак с шаблоном; металлические части дальше получаются литьём."
		"Проверка. Посмотри материал и уровень добычи в подсказке инструмента. Одна только форма кирки не означает, что ею можно добывать любую руду."
		"Булыжник не расходуется при зачёте. Часть запаса пригодится для печи в следующем задании."
	]
	quest.2101000000000003.title: "First Heat"
	quest.2101000000000003.quest_subtitle: "A furnace"
	quest.2101000000000003.quest_desc: ["Build a furnace. The world will soon demand much more metal."]
	quest.2101000000000004.title: "Iron Reserve"
	quest.2101000000000004.quest_subtitle: "8 iron ingots"
	quest.2101000000000004.quest_desc: ["Gather your first stock of iron for tools and machinery."]
	quest.2101000000000005.title: "Copper"
	quest.2101000000000005.quest_subtitle: "8 copper ingots"
	quest.2101000000000005.quest_desc: ["Copper will be used throughout Meridian's technological progression."]
	quest.2101000000000006.title: "A Foothold"
	quest.2101000000000006.quest_subtitle: "Establish a permanent base"
	quest.2101000000000006.quest_desc: ["Create a place that can genuinely be called a base."]
	task.3101000000000006.title: "The base is ready"

	quest.2201000000000001.title: "Foundry Basics"
	quest.2201000000000001.quest_subtitle: "How Productive Metalworks actually works"
	quest.2201000000000001.quest_desc: [
		"Productive Metalworks is Meridian's main metallurgy route. Metal first becomes fluid, then gets cast into a part."
		""
		"The minimum Foundry is 3x3x2. The bottom layer is heating coils. Leave an air block in the center of the upper layer and place a Foundry Controller, Foundry Tank and at least one Foundry Drain in the shell."
		""
		"A liquid-fuel Foundry using lava reaches 1500 C. That is enough for iron and copper at 1000 C, but not for every late recipe."
		""
		"Remember the chain: raw material -> heat -> molten metal -> drain -> tap -> casting table/basin -> mold -> part."
	]
	task.3201000000000001.title: "Foundry assembled"
	quest.2201000000000002.title: "Build a Working Foundry"
	quest.2201000000000002.quest_subtitle: "Controller, Tank, Drain and heating"
	quest.2201000000000002.quest_desc: [
		"Build the smallest working Foundry step by step."
		""
		"1. Make a 3x3 bottom layer of the correct heating coils."
		"2. Build the upper shell and keep the center as air."
		"3. Put the Controller, Tank and Drain into the shell."
		"4. Supply the heating system with the fuel or power it actually requires."
		""
		"If the Controller does not recognize the structure, check size, the center air block, coil type and the three mandatory Foundry blocks first."
	]
	task.3201000000000002.title: "Heater online"
	quest.2201000000000003.title: "First Melt"
	quest.2201000000000003.quest_subtitle: "Temperature is part of the recipe"
	quest.2201000000000003.quest_desc: [
		"Make your first melt and learn to read temperature requirements."
		""
		"Example: one iron ingot needs about 1000 C and produces 90 mB of molten iron. A lava-heated Foundry is hot enough for this test."
		""
		"Insert material through the Controller or drop it into the active Foundry. If it does not melt, check JEI for a valid recipe and minimum temperature."
	]
	task.3201000000000003.title: "Melt produced"
	quest.2201000000000004.title: "First Casting"
	quest.2201000000000004.quest_subtitle: "Drain, Tap and Casting Table"
	quest.2201000000000004.quest_desc: [
		"Move molten metal out of the Foundry and cast a real part."
		""
		"1. Attach a Tap to the Foundry Drain."
		"2. Put a Casting Table below it for items/parts; use a Casting Basin for blocks."
		"3. Place the mold required by the JEI recipe into the cast slot."
		"4. Open the Tap and wait for pouring and full cooling."
		""
		"A result cannot be removed while it is still cooling. If nothing pours, check the fluid, mold, required amount and block placement."
	]
	task.3201000000000004.title: "First casting complete"
	quest.2201000000000005.title: "Molds Are the Foundry's Language"
	quest.2201000000000005.quest_subtitle: "The same melt can become different parts"
	quest.2201000000000005.quest_desc: [
		"The mold determines what the same molten material becomes."
		""
		"One ingot is 90 mB and a 9-ingot block is 810 mB. Silent Gear and weapon parts can use different amounts, so read the actual JEI recipe."
		""
		"Compare at least two casting recipes for the same metal. Before opening the Tap, name the mold, required amount and expected output."
	]
	task.3201000000000005.title: "First alloy created"
	quest.2201000000000006.title: "First Alloy"
	quest.2201000000000006.quest_subtitle: "Alloying is a separate production step"
	quest.2201000000000006.quest_desc: [
		"Key alloys in Meridian use the Productive Metalworks Foundry; shortcut Mixer and Alloy Forge routes are intentionally disabled."
		""
		"Example: the Foundry's Invar demonstration uses 2 parts iron to 1 part nickel. Use the actual fluid amounts shown in JEI."
		""
		"Compatible fluids may react inside the Foundry. A Stability Upgrade completely disables automatic alloying, which is useful when melts must stay separate."
		""
		"If an alloy does not form, check ratio, temperature and whether Stability is installed."
	]
	task.3201000000000006.title: "Weapon cast"

	quest.2301000000000001.title: "Engineer's Tool"
	quest.2301000000000001.quest_subtitle: "Create wrench"
	quest.2301000000000001.quest_desc: ["Craft a wrench. There will be a lot of machinery from here on."]
	quest.2301000000000002.title: "Transmit Motion"
	quest.2301000000000002.quest_subtitle: "Cogwheels"
	quest.2301000000000002.quest_desc: ["Build a stock of cogwheels and begin a mechanical network."]
	quest.2301000000000003.title: "Mechanical Press"
	quest.2301000000000003.quest_subtitle: "First production node"
	quest.2301000000000003.quest_desc: ["Build a mechanical press."]
	quest.2301000000000004.title: "Mechanical Mixer"
	quest.2301000000000004.quest_subtitle: "Mixing and processing"
	quest.2301000000000004.quest_desc: ["Add a mechanical mixer to production."]
	quest.2301000000000005.title: "Automated Line"
	quest.2301000000000005.quest_subtitle: "Connect the processes"
	quest.2301000000000005.quest_desc: ["Link several machines into a genuinely automatic production line."]
	quest.2301000000000006.title: "Infrastructure"
	quest.2301000000000006.quest_subtitle: "Production becomes a system"
	quest.2301000000000006.quest_desc: ["Build a stable network for production and transport."]
	quest.2401000000000001.title: "Specialization"
	quest.2401000000000001.quest_subtitle: "Choose a profession"
	quest.2401000000000001.quest_desc: ["Decide how your character contributes to the settlement. A profession defines a specialty, not a backstory."]
	task.3401000000000001.title: "Profession chosen"
	quest.2401000000000002.title: "Set I"
	quest.2401000000000002.quest_subtitle: "Basic profession gear"
	quest.2401000000000002.quest_desc: ["Assemble the first tier of your profession set."]
	task.3401000000000002.title: "Set I assembled"
	quest.2401000000000003.title: "Set II"
	quest.2401000000000003.quest_subtitle: "Reinforced gear"
	quest.2401000000000003.quest_desc: ["Upgrade to the second tier."]
	task.3401000000000003.title: "Set II assembled"
	quest.2401000000000004.title: "Set III"
	quest.2401000000000004.quest_subtitle: "Technological tier"
	quest.2401000000000004.quest_desc: ["Assemble the third tier, where equipment starts strongly changing profession capabilities."]
	task.3401000000000004.title: "Set III assembled"
	quest.2401000000000005.title: "Set IV"
	quest.2401000000000005.quest_subtitle: "Maximum specialization"
	quest.2401000000000005.quest_desc: ["Create the fourth tier of the profession set."]
	task.3401000000000005.title: "Set IV assembled"

	quest.2501000000000001.title: "Nether Protection"
	quest.2501000000000001.quest_subtitle: "A personal authorized Curios ring is required"
	quest.2501000000000001.quest_desc: [
		"Nether travel requires a personal authorized ring. Merely owning an item with the correct ID is not enough."
		""
		"1. A real player must perform the final craft. Automated output is a permanently inert shell."
		"2. Check the tooltip for your operator name, IDENTIFICATION CONFIRMED and PROTECTION CIRCUIT AUTHORIZED."
		"3. Equip the ring in a Curios slot. A ring sitting in normal inventory does not authorize the portal."
		""
		"The FTB item task only confirms possession. The real portal separately checks owner data and Curios equipment."
	]
	quest.2501000000000002.title: "The Nether"
	quest.2501000000000002.quest_subtitle: "First crossing"
	quest.2501000000000002.quest_desc: ["Enter the Nether after preparing for it."]
	quest.2501000000000003.title: "Blaze"
	quest.2501000000000003.quest_subtitle: "Blaze rods"
	quest.2501000000000003.quest_desc: ["Obtain blaze rods for the path toward the End."]
	quest.2501000000000005.title: "End Protection"
	quest.2501000000000005.quest_subtitle: "A separate personal ring is required"
	quest.2501000000000005.quest_desc: [
		"The End uses a separate personal ring; the Nether ring does not replace it."
		""
		"Craft it personally, verify the authorized tooltip and equip it in a Curios slot before entering."
		""
		"End access also requires your own Nether visit history and all twelve required route eyes."
		""
		"The FTB item task confirms possession only. A foreign, inert or unequipped ring will still fail the real gate."
	]
	quest.2501000000000006.title: "The End"
	quest.2501000000000006.quest_subtitle: "The next horizon"
	quest.2501000000000006.quest_desc: ["Enter the End and advance the world's technological progression."]
	quest.2251000000000001.title: "Organized Storage"
	quest.2251000000000001.quest_subtitle: "Separate resources before the factory grows"
	quest.2251000000000001.quest_desc: [
		"Build at least four storage containers and give them clear roles: ores/metals, machinery, building materials and rare components."
		""
		"Test the layout by carrying one item from each category and putting all four away quickly. If you must open every chest to remember where things go, the system is not organized yet."
		""
		"FTB tracks the four chests; the sorting experiment is the part that actually teaches the habit."
	]
	quest.2251000000000002.title: "Backpack"
	quest.2251000000000002.quest_subtitle: "Learn storage slots and upgrade slots"
	quest.2251000000000002.quest_desc: [
		"Build a Sophisticated Backpacks backpack and learn its two main areas."
		""
		"The main inventory grid stores items. A basic leather backpack has 27 inventory slots by default."
		"The upgrade slots are separate and hold behavior modules. A basic backpack has 1 upgrade slot by default; higher tiers have more."
		""
		"Test it with one purpose-built loadout, such as food, torches and spare blocks for mining. Do not confuse normal storage slots with upgrade slots."
	]
	quest.2251000000000003.title: "Storage Upgrades"
	quest.2251000000000003.quest_subtitle: "Install, configure and test one upgrade"
	quest.2251000000000003.quest_desc: [
		"An upgrade changes storage behavior; it is not just an icon."
		""
		"Examples include Pickup, Magnet, Filter, Deposit and Refill. Install one, configure at least one rule and verify that its behavior actually changes."
		""
		"Disable or remove the upgrade and confirm the behavior disappears. That proves you know which module is doing the work."
	]
	task.3251000000000003.title: "Upgrade tested"
	quest.2251000000000004.title: "Filtering"
	quest.2251000000000004.quest_subtitle: "Test one accepted and one rejected item"
	quest.2251000000000004.quest_desc: [
		"Configure a filter using a concrete test."
		""
		"Example: allow cobblestone. Send cobblestone and an iron ingot through the same input. Cobblestone should enter the target storage while iron should be rejected or routed elsewhere."
		""
		"If everything passes, check whitelist/blacklist mode. If nothing passes, check input direction, free space and the filter entry."
	]
	task.3251000000000004.title: "Filter verified"
	quest.2251000000000005.title: "Readable Warehouse"
	quest.2251000000000005.quest_subtitle: "Storage should make sense to other players"
	quest.2251000000000005.quest_desc: [
		"Make the warehouse readable without a guided tour."
		""
		"Label sections with signs, item frames or another obvious visual system. Use broad, useful categories rather than dozens of arbitrary chest names."
		""
		"Test three targets: iron, food and mechanical parts. Another player should be able to find them without you telling them which container to open."
	]
	task.3251000000000005.title: "Warehouse organized"
	quest.2251000000000006.title: "Input and Output"
	quest.2251000000000006.quest_subtitle: "Prepare storage for automation"
	quest.2251000000000006.quest_desc: [
		"Separate where raw materials enter storage from where production consumes them."
		""
		"A simple example is an input chest for mining loot and a work buffer near the Foundry or factory line. This makes troubleshooting visible: a full input means sorting is falling behind; an empty work buffer means production is outrunning supply."
		""
		"You do not need full automation yet. Leave clear connection points for later funnels, belts, hoppers or other logistics."
	]
	task.3251000000000006.title: "Input and output separated"
	quest.2251000000000007.title: "Buffer"
	quest.2251000000000007.quest_subtitle: "Machines do not always run at the same speed"
	quest.2251000000000007.quest_desc: [
		"A buffer is intermediate storage between two stages that run at different speeds."
		""
		"Let the first stage run, stop the second stage briefly, and verify that the buffer accepts the accumulated items. Restart the second stage and watch the stored amount decrease."
		""
		"If the buffer only fills forever, it is hiding a permanent throughput mismatch rather than solving a short interruption."
	]
	task.3251000000000007.title: "Buffer online"
	quest.2251000000000008.title: "Central Warehouse"
	quest.2251000000000008.quest_subtitle: "A storage system that can grow"
	quest.2251000000000008.quest_desc: [
		"Build a central warehouse that can expand without demolishing half the room."
		""
		"Leave space for more containers, walkways and future input/output lines. Keep manual player access separate from the area where automation will connect."
		""
		"Expansion test: imagine your metal storage must double tomorrow. If you can add capacity without rebuilding the whole warehouse, the layout is doing its job."
	]
	task.3251000000000008.title: "Central warehouse online"

	quest.2351000000000001.title: "Move It Automatically"
	quest.2351000000000001.quest_subtitle: "A belt becomes a transport line"
	quest.2351000000000001.quest_desc: [
		"Для зачёта получи в обычный инвентарь 3 механических ремня. Предметы не расходуются. После открытия задания подожди несколько секунд."
		"Зачёт проверяет предметы. Сборка и работа описанного механизма автоматически не проверяются; опыт ниже помогает научиться пользоваться полученным оборудованием."
		""
		"Шаг 1. Поставь два вала параллельно: их оси должны смотреть в одну сторону. Для первого опыта расположи их на одинаковой высоте по прямой."
		"Шаг 2. Держа механический ремень, выбери первый вал, затем второй. Подай вращение на один из них."
		"Шаг 3. Брось один ненужный предмет на движущуюся поверхность и проследи, до какого конца он доедет. Сначала проверь направление, потом подключай постоянную подачу."
		"Если ремень не создаётся, уменьши расстояние и проверь ориентацию валов. Если стоит — проверь привод и перегрузку. Не соединяй его с двумя конфликтующими источниками вращения."
		""
		"Наглядно: открой Ponder нужного блока по подсказке в JEI и рассмотри стороны подключения."
	]
	quest.2351000000000002.title: "Automatic Loading"
	quest.2351000000000002.quest_subtitle: "Feed the line from storage"
	quest.2351000000000002.quest_desc: [
		"Для зачёта получи в обычный инвентарь 2 андезитовых шлюза. Предметы не расходуются. После открытия задания подожди несколько секунд."
		"Зачёт проверяет предметы. Сборка и работа описанного механизма автоматически не проверяются; опыт ниже помогает научиться пользоваться полученным оборудованием."
		""
		"Шаг 1. Поставь сундук рядом с рабочим ремнём, оставив место для андезитового шлюза на обращённой к ремню стороне."
		"Шаг 2. Через Ponder посмотри варианты установки шлюза. Настрой первый на выдачу из сундука к ремню, второй у конечного сундука — на приём."
		"Шаг 3. Положи в исходный сундук несколько предметов и проверь весь путь. Они должны попадать в конечный сундук."
		"Если предметы стоят у выхода, проверь свободные слоты конечного сундука, направление шлюза и отсутствие блокирующего сигнала. Андезитовый шлюз не заменяет латунный фильтрующий."
		""
		"Наглядно: открой Ponder нужного блока по подсказке в JEI и рассмотри стороны подключения."
	]
	quest.2351000000000003.title: "Split the Stream"
	quest.2351000000000003.quest_subtitle: "Two items, two destinations"
	quest.2351000000000003.quest_desc: [
		"Для зачёта получи в обычный инвентарь 1 фильтр предметов. Предметы не расходуются. После открытия задания подожди несколько секунд."
		"Зачёт проверяет предметы. Сборка и работа описанного механизма автоматически не проверяются; опыт ниже помогает научиться пользоваться полученным оборудованием."
		""
		"Шаг 1. Сделай фильтр и открой его интерфейс ПКМ. Добавь образцы двух разных предметов и выбери режим допуска либо запрета."
		"Шаг 2. Для применения нужен блок с настоящим слотом фильтрации: например, латунный шлюз из следующего задания. Обычный андезитовый шлюз такого слота не имеет."
		"Шаг 3. Установи подготовленный фильтр в совместимый слот и пропусти небольшую смешанную партию. Сравни, какие предметы прошли."
		"Если проходит лишнее, проверь режим допуска/запрета и параметры сопоставления фильтра. Если не проходит ничего, сначала проверь направление самого приёмника."
		""
		"Наглядно: открой Ponder нужного блока по подсказке в JEI и рассмотри стороны подключения."
	]
	quest.2351000000000004.title: "Overflow"
	quest.2351000000000004.quest_subtitle: "What happens when the main output is full?"
	quest.2351000000000004.quest_desc: [
		"Для зачёта получи в обычный инвентарь 2 латунных шлюза. Предметы не расходуются. После открытия задания подожди несколько секунд."
		"Зачёт проверяет предметы. Сборка и работа описанного механизма автоматически не проверяются; опыт ниже помогает научиться пользоваться полученным оборудованием."
		""
		"Шаг 1. Получи латунь по цепочке Foundry и сделай латунные шлюзы по JEI. Подготовь движущийся ремень и два сундука-приёмника."
		"Шаг 2. Поставь у каждого приёмника латунный шлюз. В их фильтрующих слотах задай разные предметы: например, железные и медные слитки."
		"Шаг 3. Подай маленькую смешанную партию. Убедись, что каждый приёмник принимает только свой материал."
		"Шаг 4. Временно заполни один сундук и посмотри, где задерживается его поток. Фильтр выбирает допустимый предмет, но сам по себе не создаёт запасной маршрут."
		"Для простого остаточного потока поставь дальше по ремню отдельный приёмник без фильтра. Не допускай возврата неразобранных предметов на вход бесконечным кругом."
		""
		"Наглядно: открой Ponder нужного блока по подсказке в JEI и рассмотри стороны подключения."
	]
	quest.2351000000000005.title: "Fluids"
	quest.2351000000000005.quest_subtitle: "Pipes are logistics too"
	quest.2351000000000005.quest_desc: [
		"Для зачёта получи в обычный инвентарь 8 жидкостных труб. Предметы не расходуются. После открытия задания подожди несколько секунд."
		"Зачёт проверяет предметы. Сборка и работа описанного механизма автоматически не проверяются; опыт ниже помогает научиться пользоваться полученным оборудованием."
		""
		"Шаг 1. Наметь короткий путь между источником воды и ёмкостью. Соедини их жидкостными трубами, оставив участок под механическую помпу."
		"Шаг 2. Труба сама не создаёт поток и не служит баком. В следующем задании добавишь помпу и вращение."
		"Шаг 3. Проверь, что конец у источника действительно может забрать воду, а конец у приёмника касается совместимого входа ёмкости."
		"Если потом поток не появится, проверь не только целостность трубы, но и источник, свободный объём приёмника и направление помпы. Разные жидкости проверяй на отдельных линиях."
		""
		"Наглядно: открой Ponder нужного блока по подсказке в JEI и рассмотри стороны подключения."
	]
	quest.2351000000000006.title: "Separate Pipe Networks"
	quest.2351000000000006.quest_subtitle: "Make different fluid routes obvious"
	quest.2351000000000006.quest_desc: [
		"Для зачёта получи в обычный инвентарь 1 механическую помпу. Предметы не расходуются. После открытия задания подожди несколько секунд."
		"Зачёт проверяет предметы. Сборка и работа описанного механизма автоматически не проверяются; опыт ниже помогает научиться пользоваться полученным оборудованием."
		""
		"Шаг 1. Встрой механическую помпу в подготовленный водяной трубопровод и подай вращение на её вал."
		"Шаг 2. Стрелка должна смотреть от источника к приёмнику. Направление потока меняется гаечным ключом; изменение направления вращения само по себе не разворачивает перекачку."
		"Шаг 3. Для проверки используй короткую линию и воду. Наблюдай, как растёт уровень в принимающем баке."
		"Если перекачка остановилась, проверь наличие воды, заполнение бака и привод. Одна помпа действует на ограниченную длину труб; длинную сеть разделяй дополнительными помпами."
		"Цветные трубы — отдельное расширение. Две независимые линии сначала научись разделять физически: обычная помпа не окрашивает и не фильтрует жидкость."
		""
		"Наглядно: открой Ponder нужного блока по подсказке в JEI и рассмотри стороны подключения."
	]
	quest.2351000000000007.title: "Production Line"
	quest.2351000000000007.quest_subtitle: "Raw material in, product out"
	quest.2351000000000007.quest_desc: [
		"Для зачёта получи в обычный инвентарь 6 механических ремней, 2 андезитовых шлюза и 1 фильтр предметов. Предметы не расходуются. После открытия задания подожди несколько секунд."
		"Зачёт проверяет предметы. Сборка и работа описанного механизма автоматически не проверяются; опыт ниже помогает научиться пользоваться полученным оборудованием."
		""
		"Шаг 1. Выбери один доступный рецепт механического пресса в JEI. Подготовь только небольшую партию его исходного материала."
		"Шаг 2. Соедини входной сундук, ремень под прессом и выходной сундук. Подведи вращение к ремню и прессу."
		"Шаг 3. Пропусти один предмет. Он должен пройти нужную обработку и попасть в выходной сундук. После этого подай небольшую партию."
		"Шаг 4. Если нужны фильтры, используй латунные шлюзы или другие совместимые блоки. Андезитовые шлюзы из комплекта годятся для простого ввода/вывода, но не принимают фильтр."
		"Если сырьё уезжает необработанным, проверь рецепт, положение пресса над ремнём и его вращение. Если предмет остановился, проверь выход и свободное место."
		""
		"Наглядно: открой Ponder нужного блока по подсказке в JEI и рассмотри стороны подключения."
	]
	quest.2351000000000008.title: "Find the Bottleneck"
	quest.2351000000000008.quest_subtitle: "Good automation is understandable"
	quest.2351000000000008.quest_desc: [
		"Для зачёта получи в обычный инвентарь 1 умный жёлоб. Предметы не расходуются. После открытия задания подожди несколько секунд."
		"Зачёт проверяет предметы. Сборка и работа описанного механизма автоматически не проверяются; опыт ниже помогает научиться пользоваться полученным оборудованием."
		""
		"Шаг 1. Найди умный жёлоб в JEI и открой Ponder. Он нужен для контролируемой вертикальной передачи предметов и поддерживает фильтрацию."
		"Шаг 2. Для первого опыта поставь его между верхним и нижним хранилищем. Настрой фильтр на один из двух тестовых предметов."
		"Шаг 3. Положи оба предмета сверху. Проверь, что вниз проходит выбранный материал, а второй остаётся в источнике."
		"Шаг 4. Заполни нижний инвентарь и проверь остановку передачи. Освободи место: поток должен возобновиться."
		"При поиске затора проверяй путь от конца к началу: заполненный приёмник, фильтр, сигнал блокировки, затем источник. Изменяй по одному условию за раз."
		""
		"Наглядно: открой Ponder нужного блока по подсказке в JEI и рассмотри стороны подключения."
	]
	quest.2375000000000001.title: "Boiler Body"
	quest.2375000000000001.quest_subtitle: "Fluid Tanks form the boiler"
	quest.2375000000000001.quest_desc: ["Prepare several Fluid Tanks. A Create steam boiler is assembled from tanks rather than crafted as one block."]
	quest.2375000000000002.title: "Fluid Pipes"
	quest.2375000000000002.quest_subtitle: "Give water a path"
	quest.2375000000000002.quest_desc: ["Prepare Fluid Pipes for a continuous water supply."]
	quest.2375000000000003.title: "Mechanical Pump"
	quest.2375000000000003.quest_subtitle: "Move water in the correct direction"
	quest.2375000000000003.quest_desc: ["A Mechanical Pump requires rotation and determines the direction of fluid flow."]
	quest.2375000000000004.title: "Heat Source"
	quest.2375000000000004.quest_subtitle: "Steam requires a captured Blaze"
	quest.2375000000000004.quest_desc: ["Prepare for a Blaze Burner. Capture a live Blaze with an empty burner; the Blaze Rod task only tracks that you have reached the relevant Nether stage."]
	quest.2375000000000005.title: "Steam Engine"
	quest.2375000000000005.quest_subtitle: "Turn boiler output into rotation"
	quest.2375000000000005.quest_desc: ["Attach a Steam Engine to a working boiler and connect its output to a shaft."]
	quest.2375000000000006.title: "Stressometer"
	quest.2375000000000006.quest_subtitle: "Measure the mechanical network"
	quest.2375000000000006.quest_desc: ["Use a Stressometer to watch SU usage and available capacity."]
	quest.2375000000000007.title: "Engineer's Goggles"
	quest.2375000000000007.quest_subtitle: "Read technical information directly"
	quest.2375000000000007.quest_desc: [
		"Engineer's Goggles turn 'the network feels overloaded' into readable information."
		""
		"Create rotation speed and load are different values: RPM is speed, while stress capacity and stress impact describe how much load the network can supply and consume."
		""
		"Wear the goggles, read a Stressometer, connect one more machine and compare the remaining capacity. Use those numbers before deciding that a steam plant needs another engine."
	]
	quest.2375000000000008.title: "Steam Plant"
	quest.2375000000000008.quest_subtitle: "Prepare a practical first boiler"
	quest.2375000000000008.quest_desc: ["The task tracks only reliable inventory milestones: 9 Fluid Tanks, 2 Steam Engines and a Mechanical Pump. Assemble them with water supply and heat into a working steam system."]

	quest.2425000000000001.title: "Magnetic Field"
	quest.2425000000000001.quest_subtitle: "Electricity starts with the generator"
	quest.2425000000000001.quest_desc: ["Prepare Magnetite Blocks. Magnets around a Generator Coil determine conversion efficiency."]
	quest.2425000000000002.title: "Generator Coil"
	quest.2425000000000002.quest_subtitle: "Convert rotation into electricity"
	quest.2425000000000002.quest_desc: ["Rotate a Generator Coil and surround it with magnets."]
	quest.2425000000000003.title: "Carbon Brushes"
	quest.2425000000000003.quest_subtitle: "Collect generated electricity"
	quest.2425000000000003.quest_desc: [
		"Carbon Brushes collect electrical power from a working Generator Coil. A spinning coil without correctly placed brushes is not yet a usable network source."
		""
		"First provide Create rotation to the coil, then verify the magnets around it, then place the brushes so they can collect the generated energy."
		""
		"If the coil does not rotate, diagnose the mechanical drive. If it rotates but produces no usable power, check magnets and brush contact before blaming the connectors or motor."
	]
	quest.2425000000000004.title: "Electrical Connector"
	quest.2425000000000004.quest_subtitle: "Connect source and consumer with a wire"
	quest.2425000000000004.quest_desc: [
		"An Electrical Connector is a network endpoint. A single connector does not create a network; endpoints must be linked with wire."
		""
		"1. Put one connector next to the source and another next to the consumer."
		"2. Link them with wire. The default maximum length of one connection is 16 blocks."
		"3. If the source is an energy storage, set its connector to PULL with the wrench. INERT does not actively extract energy."
		"4. Consumers do not need a separate Push mode."
		""
		"For troubleshooting, verify the wire first, then PULL at the source, then the consumer itself."
	]
	quest.2425000000000005.title: "Electric Motor"
	quest.2425000000000005.quest_subtitle: "Turn electricity back into rotation"
	quest.2425000000000005.quest_desc: ["Supply a Basic Motor with electricity and connect its rotational output to a shaft."]
	quest.2425000000000006.title: "Motor Extension"
	quest.2425000000000006.quest_subtitle: "More mechanical capacity costs more electricity"
	quest.2425000000000006.quest_desc: ["A motor extension increases available stress capacity and raises electrical consumption."]
	quest.2425000000000007.title: "Energiser"
	quest.2425000000000007.quest_subtitle: "Electricity and rotation in one process"
	quest.2425000000000007.quest_desc: ["The Energiser requires both electrical energy and rotation to process items on a depot or belt."]
	quest.2425000000000008.title: "Close the Energy Loop"
	quest.2425000000000008.quest_subtitle: "Rotation -> electricity -> rotation"
	quest.2425000000000008.quest_desc: [
		"Build and test the full learning chain:"
		""
		"SU source -> generator coil + magnets -> carbon brushes -> connector -> wire -> connector -> electric motor -> shaft"
		""
		"Test it in stages: first coil rotation, then magnets and brushes, then the wire link and source-side PULL, and only then the motor and mechanical load."
		""
		"The quest can detect the components you own, not the correctness of the structure. A good proof is simple: breaking the wire should stop the powered motor."
	]


	quest.2481000000000001.title: "Physics Assembler"
	quest.2481000000000001.quest_subtitle: "Learn physical contraptions before building an aircraft"
	quest.2481000000000001.quest_desc: [
		"The Physics Assembler turns a glued block structure into a real Simulated physical contraption."
		""
		"Build a small test platform, connect it with Super Glue or Honey Glue, and assemble it through the Ponder procedure. Diagonal-edge connections can become part of the same physical structure, so inspect the glued boundary first."
		""
		"After assembly the blocks remain interactive. For disassembly, stop the body and bring it close to terrain; excessive speed, tilt or poor grid alignment can prevent safe placement back into blocks."
		""
		"Practice the full cycle once: assemble, move slightly, stop, and disassemble."
	]

	quest.2481000000000002.title: "Swivel Bearing"
	quest.2481000000000002.quest_subtitle: "A rotating joint that can pass rotational power through itself"
	quest.2481000000000002.quest_desc: [
		"The Swivel Bearing assembles a glued structure in front of it and allows that physical section to rotate."
		""
		"Rotational power can pass through the center shaft while the bearing itself turns. Redstone can unlock the joint for free rotation, with the lock behavior configurable through the value panel."
		""
		"Test it with a shaft entering one side and a mechanism on the other. Rotate the joint and verify the downstream mechanism keeps receiving rotation."
	]

	quest.2481000000000003.title: "Rope System"
	quest.2481000000000003.quest_subtitle: "Winch, connectors and a physical link between bodies"
	quest.2481000000000003.quest_desc: [
		"Make Rope Couplings, a Rope Winch and two Rope Connectors."
		""
		"A Winch can connect to a Connector, and two Connectors can link to each other. Two Winches cannot be linked directly."
		""
		"Rotating the Winch reels the rope in or out. Shears remove rope links, and a wrench can be used while sliding along a rope."
		""
		"Build a short lifting test: suspend a small load, raise it, then lower it again."
	]

	quest.2481000000000004.title: "Docking Connectors"
	quest.2481000000000004.quest_subtitle: "Join two contraptions without turning them into one body"
	quest.2481000000000004.quest_desc: [
		"Build two Docking Connectors and place them facing each other on separate physical contraptions."
		""
		"Extended connectors try to align automatically. When alignment is sufficient they create a rigid joint, while both sides remain separate physical bodies."
		""
		"Items and fluids can pass through a dock, but insertion and extraction still need to be arranged on both sides. Retracting either connector undocks the pair; a comparator can report docking progress."
	]

	quest.2481000000000005.title: "Portable Engine"
	quest.2481000000000005.quest_subtitle: "Local rotational power on a moving physical contraption"
	quest.2481000000000005.quest_desc: [
		"Build a Portable Engine of any color. Because the engine has many color variants, this lesson uses a manual checkmark after the real test rather than forcing one item ID."
		""
		"The engine burns fuel to create rotational force and can be configured for either direction. Fuel can be automated."
		""
		"Install one on a small physical contraption, fuel it, connect a shaft, and verify the shaft rotates without a stationary external network."
		""
		"A Blaze Cake can superheat the engine for more output; test normal operation first."
	]
	task.3481000000000005.title: "Portable Engine tested"

	quest.2481000000000006.title: "Altitude, Velocity and Tilt"
	quest.2481000000000006.quest_subtitle: "Three sensors instead of flying by guesswork"
	quest.2481000000000006.quest_desc: [
		"Build an Altitude Sensor, Velocity Sensor and Gimbal Sensor."
		""
		"The Altitude Sensor converts height into redstone and, with Engineer's Goggles, also exposes exact altitude and air pressure. The Velocity Sensor measures only the velocity component along its facing axis. The Gimbal Sensor reacts to orientation, with its axes handled independently."
		""
		"Mount all three on a small test body. Raise it, move along the velocity sensor axis, and tilt it slightly so each sensor can be observed reacting to its own quantity."
	]

	quest.2481000000000007.title: "Vision and Navigation"
	quest.2481000000000007.quest_subtitle: "Detect obstacles and point toward a target"
	quest.2481000000000007.quest_desc: [
		"An Optical Sensor detects blocks interrupting its laser path and outputs a distance-based redstone signal. A filter can limit which blocks count."
		""
		"A Navigation Table accepts a navigation target item and outputs redstone toward that target while accounting for the real rotation of a moving physical contraption."
		""
		"Test the sensor with a removable obstacle, then place a valid target in the Navigation Table and slowly rotate the platform to watch the directional output change."
	]

	quest.2481000000000008.title: "Propeller Bearing"
	quest.2481000000000008.quest_subtitle: "Thrust comes from a valid propeller, not RPM alone"
	quest.2481000000000008.quest_desc: [
		"The Propeller Bearing assembles the structure in front of it into a propeller and creates thrust."
		""
		"A valid propeller needs at least two sail-like blocks. More useful sail area increases thrust nonlinearly and also increases mechanical load."
		""
		"Reversing rotation reverses thrust. Engineer's Goggles show thrust and airflow."
		""
		"Build a small propeller, record its readings, enlarge it and compare both thrust and Create stress load."
	]

	quest.2481000000000009.title: "Small Propellers"
	quest.2481000000000009.quest_subtitle: "Compact thrust without a large sail rotor"
	quest.2481000000000009.quest_desc: [
		"Build a Wooden Propeller and an Andesite Propeller."
		""
		"Small propellers are useful when a full Propeller Bearing rotor does not fit. Test one on a small platform at a fixed rotational speed, then reverse the rotation and verify the thrust direction changes."
		""
		"Multiple propellers do not automatically make a stable craft: asymmetric thrust around the center of mass can rotate the whole body."
	]

	quest.2481000000000010.title: "Gyroscopic Propeller Bearing"
	quest.2481000000000010.quest_subtitle: "Thrust attempts to stay aligned to local gravity"
	quest.2481000000000010.quest_desc: [
		"The Gyroscopic Propeller Bearing automatically adjusts a limited thrust angle to stabilize orientation relative to local gravity."
		""
		"Its tilt range and response speed are limited, and very low RPM reduces its ability to correct. A redstone signal returns it toward its original block normal."
		""
		"Compare a normal and gyroscopic bearing on similar small platforms and observe how their thrust directions react to a small change in body orientation."
	]

	quest.2481000000000011.title: "Balloon Envelope"
	quest.2481000000000011.quest_subtitle: "Lift needs an enclosed volume, not just a burner"
	quest.2481000000000011.quest_desc: [
		"Build at least eight Envelope blocks and a Balloon Burner."
		""
		"Envelope blocks must enclose a volume. Hot air fills that volume from the source, while leaks destroy the useful gas volume. Blocks inside the envelope reduce available volume."
		""
		"Build a small sealed test balloon, activate the burner and observe lift. Then deliberately open one envelope block and compare the behavior."
	]

	quest.2481000000000012.title: "Steam Vent"
	quest.2481000000000012.quest_subtitle: "A steam boiler can become a source of lift"
	quest.2481000000000012.quest_desc: [
		"The Steam Vent fills a balloon with steam using familiar boiler infrastructure."
		""
		"It needs adequate heat, water and boiler output. Redstone strength controls the target fill percentage, and multiple vents can contribute to one envelope."
		""
		"Connect one vent to a working steam setup and sealed envelope. Start with a low signal and increase it in steps while observing filling and lift."
	]

	quest.2481000000000016.title: "Smart Propeller"
	quest.2481000000000016.quest_subtitle: "Compact thrust with self-leveling behavior"
	quest.2481000000000016.quest_desc: [
		"The Smart Propeller creates thrust while also trying to correct its own tilt on one axis."
		""
		"A wrench can change its thrust direction. Test it on a small tilting platform with stable rotational input and watch the propeller itself react to body angle."
		""
		"It is an actuator, not an autopilot: controlled flight still needs sensors and logic."
	]

	quest.2481000000000017.title: "Steering and Control"
	quest.2481000000000017.quest_subtitle: "Connect player input, sensors and actuators"
	quest.2481000000000017.quest_desc: [
		"Build a Steering Wheel and create a simple control chain for a physical craft."
		""
		"Start with one player command, one sensor and one actuator rather than a complicated aircraft."
		""
		"For example, a steering command changes thrust behavior while a Gimbal Sensor shows the resulting tilt and an Altitude Sensor reports whether the craft is climbing or descending."
		""
		"When every input produces a predictable reaction you can explain from sensor readings, the craft is ready for a test flight."
	]

	quest.2481000000000013.title: "Controlled Test Flight"
	quest.2481000000000013.quest_subtitle: "Low, slow and with a known way to stop"
	quest.2481000000000013.quest_desc: [
		"Build a small controllable physical craft using the systems learned in this chapter."
		""
		"Before launch, check glue connectivity, center of mass, thrust direction, mechanical capacity, fuel and sensor readings. Keep a reliable way to remove thrust completely."
		""
		"Perform the first flight close to the ground with no cargo: lift slightly, stabilize, make a short horizontal movement, turn or redirect, return and land."
		""
		"Only attempt disassembly after the body is fully stopped. Mark the task complete after the craft flies and lands without emergency destruction."
	]
	task.3481000000000013.title: "Controlled test flight completed"

	quest.2481000000000014.title: "Wheel Mount"
	quest.2481000000000014.quest_subtitle: "Offroad converts Create rotation into ground movement"
	quest.2481000000000014.quest_desc: [
		"Build two Wheel Mounts and two standard Tires."
		""
		"A tire is installed on the front of the mount. Without a Tire-like item the mount does not act as a physical wheel."
		""
		"Create rotation becomes forward drive. Redstone from above acts as braking, while side signals steer."
		""
		"Build a simple two-wheel cart and separately test low-speed drive, top-signal braking and side-signal steering."
	]

	quest.2481000000000015.title: "Borehead Bearing"
	quest.2481000000000015.quest_subtitle: "A physical mining machine also needs storage"
	quest.2481000000000015.quest_desc: [
		"Build a Borehead Bearing and at least two Rock Cutting Wheels."
		""
		"Rock Cutting Wheels mine an area around themselves rather than only one block directly ahead. Mined items enter attached storage."
		""
		"A full storage system intentionally stalls the borehead. Free space or extract items through the bearing to resume operation."
		""
		"Mining slows as one bearing must break more blocks at once; multiple bearings can divide the load. Run a short safe test and verify items actually reach storage."
	]

	quest.2511000000000001.title: "Sands of the Past"
	quest.2511000000000001.quest_subtitle: "Hint: Desert Pyramid"
	quest.2511000000000001.quest_desc: ["Search Desert Pyramid chests for this eye."]
	quest.2511000000000002.title: "Redstone Under Vines"
	quest.2511000000000002.quest_subtitle: "Hint: Jungle Temple"
	quest.2511000000000002.quest_desc: ["Search Jungle Temple chests for this eye."]
	quest.2511000000000003.title: "Under the Snow"
	quest.2511000000000003.quest_subtitle: "Hint: Igloo"
	quest.2511000000000003.quest_desc: ["Search Igloo chests for this eye."]
	quest.2511000000000004.title: "Foreign Watch"
	quest.2511000000000004.quest_subtitle: "Hint: Pillager Outpost"
	quest.2511000000000004.quest_desc: ["Search Pillager Outpost chests for this eye."]
	quest.2511000000000005.title: "What the Sea Did Not Take"
	quest.2511000000000005.quest_subtitle: "Hint: Buried Treasure"
	quest.2511000000000005.quest_desc: ["Search Buried Treasure chests for this eye."]
	quest.2511000000000006.title: "Forgotten Tunnels"
	quest.2511000000000006.quest_subtitle: "Hint: Abandoned Mineshaft"
	quest.2511000000000006.quest_desc: ["Search minecart chests in Abandoned Mineshafts."]
	quest.2511000000000007.title: "Evoker's Gaze"
	quest.2511000000000007.quest_subtitle: "Hint: Evoker"
	quest.2511000000000007.quest_desc: ["Defeat an Evoker to obtain this eye."]
	quest.2511000000000008.title: "From the Ocean Floor"
	quest.2511000000000008.quest_subtitle: "Hint: Elder Guardian"
	quest.2511000000000008.quest_desc: ["Defeat an Elder Guardian to obtain this eye."]
	quest.2511000000000009.title: "Behind Fortress Walls"
	quest.2511000000000009.quest_subtitle: "Hint: Nether Fortress"
	quest.2511000000000009.quest_desc: ["Search Nether Fortress chests for this eye."]
	quest.2511000000000010.title: "Bastion Treasure"
	quest.2511000000000010.quest_subtitle: "Hint: Treasure Bastion"
	quest.2511000000000010.quest_desc: ["Search Bastion Treasure chests for this eye."]
	quest.2511000000000011.title: "Made Calamity"
	quest.2511000000000011.quest_subtitle: "Hint: Wither"
	quest.2511000000000011.quest_desc: ["Summon and defeat the Wither to obtain this eye."]
	quest.2511000000000012.title: "Ominous Trial"
	quest.2511000000000012.quest_subtitle: "Hint: Ominous Trial Chamber reward"
	quest.2511000000000012.quest_desc: ["Search the rare ominous reward loot in Trial Chambers. This is Meridian's custom source for the Trial Eye."]

	quest.2450000000000001.title: "Forge Bench"
	quest.2450000000000001.quest_subtitle: "Modify equipment instead of constantly replacing it"
	quest.2450000000000001.quest_desc: ["Craft the Meridian Forge Bench and inspect the available modifier slots on supported equipment."]
	quest.2450000000000002.title: "Base Abrasive"
	quest.2450000000000002.quest_subtitle: "The first forging consumable"
	quest.2450000000000002.quest_desc: ["Craft Base Abrasive from flint and sand for early modifier levels."]
	quest.2450000000000003.title: "First Modifier"
	quest.2450000000000003.quest_subtitle: "Install one compatible modifier"
	quest.2450000000000003.quest_desc: ["Install a compatible modifier on a supported item. This is manually confirmed because modifier state is stored inside the item data."]
	task.3450000000000003.title: "Modifier installed"
	quest.2450000000000004.title: "Industrial Abrasive"
	quest.2450000000000004.quest_subtitle: "More serious processing"
	quest.2450000000000004.quest_desc: ["Craft Industrial Abrasive from amethyst and flint."]
	quest.2450000000000005.title: "Heat-Resistant Binder"
	quest.2450000000000005.quest_subtitle: "Nether materials unlock higher tiers"
	quest.2450000000000005.quest_desc: ["Craft Heat-Resistant Binder from magma cream and blaze powder."]
	quest.2450000000000006.title: "Finishing Abrasive"
	quest.2450000000000006.quest_subtitle: "Late-game finishing material"
	quest.2450000000000006.quest_desc: ["Craft Finishing Abrasive from popped chorus fruit and amethyst."]
	quest.2450000000000007.title: "Build a Specialization"
	quest.2450000000000007.quest_subtitle: "Use slots deliberately"
	quest.2450000000000007.quest_desc: ["Build one item with several deliberate, compatible modifiers rather than filling slots randomly."]
	task.3450000000000007.title: "Specialized item ready"

	quest.24010100000000.title: "Шахтёр • I"
	quest.24010100000000.quest_subtitle: "Build a complete profession set"
	quest.24010100000000.quest_desc: ["Profession bonuses require all four matching pieces. Mixed tiers work, but the lowest equipped tier determines the effective set tier. Normal tier upgrades preserve the armor material."]
